      "duplicates_with": {
        "tool": "ruff",
        "reason": "aislop's `lint` engine does not bundle ruff: `resolveToolBinary('ruff')` falls back to a project venv, then PATH, then a bundled tools/bin/ruff that the package does not ship (verified 2026-10-28: tools/ contains only jb/). Measured on narrative-nexus, PATH with ~/.local/bin produced 287 ruff/* findings and PATH without it produced 0 — so every aislop ruff finding is the ambient ruff on PATH. Pinning that engine means pinning PATH, so `telemetry_env.PATH` puts the prefix's python/bin first and both names then report the same pinned binary. mergeDuplicates collapses the overlap by (path, line bucket, category), crediting both tools on one finding."
      },
